has run out, open a dispute from the job's card. Our team reviews both sides and can release the payment to either party or split it; if the two of you don't settle it in the dispute window, our team decides it.`]},{id:`charged-too-much`,title:`I was charged too much`,steps:[`Open You › Money › Receipts and find the charge. A job charge is the job price (plus any urgent bonus you added), Louisiana sales tax on the labor for taxable job types, and, on your first paid job, ${f}.`,`On Declutter, the buyer pays the item price plus a buyer's fee of ${l}, once per checkout.`,`If the receipt doesn't match what you were told, contact support below with the receipt. If the mistake was ours, you get everything back.`]},{id:`item-never-came`,title:`My item never came`,steps:[`Open the order under Declutter › Buying. Every pickup or delivery happens within 7 days of paying.`,`If no Helpr takes a delivery within 48 hours, what you paid for delivery comes back, and you pick it up at the seller's door or cancel the sale for a refund.`,`If the seller doesn't show, report a problem from the order before the sale is final. The money stays held while we look at both sides, and a seller who doesn't show means everything back at the seller's cost.`]}],g=[{label:`Getting Started`,desc:`New to Helpr? Start here.`},{label:`Declutter`,desc:`Buying, selling, pickup, delivery and refunds.`},{label:`Posting a Job`,desc:`Write a great post and get results.`},{label:`Finding Work`,desc:`Apply, get hired, and grow your income.`},{label:`Payments & how your money is held`,desc:`How money is held, released, and paid.`},{label:`Trust & Safety`,desc:`Something went wrong with a job? Disputes, reporting, and ID checks.`},{label:`Account & Settings`,desc:`Email, password, deletion, bigger text.`}],_=[{topic:`Getting Started`,items:[{q:`Do I need an account to browse jobs?`,get a(){return e()?`No, you can browse without signing up. To post a job or apply for one you'll need an account with a confirmed email. We ask for your ID once: when you send a Helpr an offer, when you're hired, or when you take a delivery. Buying, selling and free items on Declutter never ask for it.`:`No, you can browse without signing up. To post a job or apply for one you'll need an account with a confirmed email.`}},{q:`Is Helpr available everywhere in Louisiana?`,a:`We're growing across Louisiana's 64 parishes. If your area isn't busy yet, posting a job is the best way to attract local Helprs.`},{q:`Can I both post jobs and do them?`,a:`Yes — every account can do both. There's no separate "poster" or "Helpr" mode.`},{q:`Can I give things away on Declutter?`,a:`Yes. Tap Sell, then "More ways to sell", then "Give away free". Neighbors tap "Ask for it", you pick who gets it, and they pick it up from your porch. Nothing is charged to either of you, and each person can ask for or hold up to 3 free items at a time.`},{q:`Can I trade on Declutter?`,a:`Yes, when the seller marks a listing "Open to trades". Offer one of your own live listings for it, item for item: no money changes hands and no fee is charged. The seller has 48 hours to accept or say no. Once accepted, each of you sets up the pickup of the other's item within 48 hours, from the porch or at the door, whichever that listing offers. If either side runs out of time or backs out before a pickup is booked, the trade ends and nobody gets a strike. Free items can't be traded.`}]},{topic:`Declutter`,items:[{q:`How do I buy something on Declutter?`,a:`Tap Buy now to pay the price, or send the seller a private offer of at least half of today's price. It isn't an auction: the item goes to the first buyer whose purchase or offer is accepted and who then pays. After you tap Buy now the item is held for you for 30 minutes while you check out; when your offer is accepted you have 24 hours. You see one total before you pay, delivery included. Missing the checkout on an accepted offer is a Declutter strike; a Buy now you don't pay for just goes back on sale.`},{q:`How do I sell?`,a:`List your own used household things with 1 to 12 photos you took, a price from $1 to $1,000 and a private lowest price you'll accept. The listing goes live when you post it. Buyers see your area name, never your address. Price drops start on: an unsold item's price drops each evening by 5%, stopping above your lowest price. You can pick a bigger step (up to 20%) or turn drops off in Declutter settings. You set up payouts with Stripe at your first paid sale, and you receive the whole item price: the buyer pays a buyer's fee of ${l} on top, once per checkout.`},{q:`How do I get the item?`,a:`Each listing says which of these it offers, with the same names as the Filters: Porch pickup (the seller leaves it out and posts a photo), Meet at a safe spot (a public place, no home address shared), Helpr delivery, or Seller delivers when the seller offers it. Shipping isn't offered. Every pickup or delivery happens within 7 days of paying, and for a pickup at the seller's place you get the exact address right after you pay. If no Helpr takes a delivery within 48 hours, what you paid for delivery comes back, and you pick it up at the seller's door or cancel the sale for a refund.`},{q:`What if something's wrong with my item?`,a:`You have 24 hours after pickup to ask the seller for a refund: they can refund all of it, offer part, or decline, and then you can report a problem for us to decide. Either of you can report a problem until the sale is final, and the money stays held while we look at both sides. An item that isn't as described, or a seller who doesn't show, means everything back at the seller's cost. Once the sale is final the item is yours as is.`},{q:`Can I deliver Declutter items?`,a:`Yes, if you're 18 or older, not banned, have fewer than 3 Declutter strikes and aren't the buyer or seller. You see your take-home pay before you take a delivery, pick the pickup time, take a photo at pickup and at the door. Large items need a truck; extra-large items a truck and a second person. You set up payouts after you take your first delivery.`}]},{topic:`Posting a Job`,items:[{q:`What should I write in my job description?`,a:`The more specific, the better. Include the exact job, how long you expect it to take, any equipment needed, and whether parking is available.`},{q:`How is the price determined?`,a:`You set the price. Pick what the job is worth to you.`},{q:`How do I cancel a job?`,a:`Open the job and tap Cancel job. ${a} With a Helpr hired, there is no charge to cancel up to 24 hours before the start. Closer than that, the Helpr gets part of the price for holding the time, and it counts as a strike. You see the exact amount before you confirm.`},{q:`What if my Helpr doesn't show up?`,a:`From 30 minutes after the start time, open the job and tap Report no-show. The Helpr comes off your job and it goes on their record. To hire someone else, change the date right away; otherwise the job is cancelled and refunded. Our team is told about every no-show.`},{q:`Can I cancel after someone applies?`,a:`Yes. ${a} After you accept a Helpr, cancelling works the same up to 24 hours before the start, with no strike. Closer than that, the Helpr also gets part of the price for holding the time, and it counts as a strike. You'll see the exact amount first.`}]},{topic:`Finding Work`,items:[{q:`How do I get my first application accepted?`,a:`A complete profile (photo, bio, skills) helps people trust you faster. Respond fast — they notice quick turnaround.`},{q:`When do I get paid?`,a:`You're paid 3 days after the person who posted the job approves it. Your bank shows it ${n}. ${f.charAt(0).toUpperCase()}${f.slice(1)} comes out of your first payout, unless you already paid it on a job you posted.`},{q:`What if the person who posted the job doesn't confirm completion?`,a:`Your payment stays held. If the person who posted the job hasn't approved it or asked for a change within 24 hours of you marking the work done, Helpr support steps in to resolve it. Once it's approved, your payout is sent ${t}.`}]},{topic:`Payments & how your money is held`,items:[{q:`How does Louisiana Helpr hold my payment?`,a:`A card is held or saved when the job is posted and charged when a Helpr accepts the offer; a bank payment or gift is paid when the job is posted. Louisiana Helpr holds that money (via Stripe) until the job is done, and you're paid ${t}. Neither side can touch it mid-job.`},{q:`What fees does Helpr charge?`,a:`When you post a job, you pay the job price (including any urgent bonus you add), plus Louisiana sales tax on the labor for taxable job types (auto and appliance repair). Your first paid job also carries ${f}, charged once per account, unless you already paid it on a job you did. On Declutter, the buyer pays the item price plus a buyer's fee of ${l}, once per checkout, and the seller keeps the whole item price. When you do a job, every job shows exactly what you will take home before you apply. Job payouts are rounded down to the whole dollar (tips are paid in full). If a paid job is cancelled, the cancel screen shows exactly what you will get back before you confirm. If the mistake was ours, you get everything back.`},{q:`What if there's a dispute?`,a:`Open a dispute from the job's card: Jobs > Working for a job you're doing, or Jobs > Posted for a job you posted. On a job you're doing, Report a Problem is there from On the way until the person who posted the job approves it, including during a revision. On a job you posted, ask for a change first and give the person doing it time to fix it; the dispute link appears once that time has run out. The person who posted the job has 24 hours after the work is marked done to approve it or ask for a change. ${u} While a dispute is open, our team reviews both sides and can release the payment to either party or split it. Disputes have a 72-hour window: if it isn't settled or escalated in that time, our team decides it, and the payment stays on hold until we do.`}]},{topic:`Trust & Safety`,items:[{q:`How are Helprs verified?`,a:`Helprs can upload trade licenses and insurance, and verified badges show on their profile. On trade jobs (${d}) you also choose who may apply: open to anyone, licensed pros only, or licensed and insured. Only Helprs who meet your choice can apply. Other categories are open to any Helpr.`},{q:`What does the cancellation rate on a profile mean?`,a:`We show a Helpr's cancellation history on their profile once they've been part of 5 or more jobs, counting both sides and any outcome. Low cancellation is a strong trust signal.`},{q:`Can I report the other person on a job?`,a:`Yes — the "Report" option is in every job detail and profile. We review every report.`}]},{topic:`Account & Settings`,items:[{q:`How do I change my email or password?`,a:`Go to You › Settings › Account and security.`},{q:`Can I delete my account?`,a:`Yes. Go to You › Settings: "Delete account" is under Your account. We ask for your password, or a code we email you, to confirm it's you. Finish or cancel any active job first: we can't delete an account while money is still being held. We retain transaction records per Louisiana law but remove all personal data.`},{q:`How do I make the text and buttons bigger?`,a:`Turn on Bigger text and buttons in You › Settings. It makes the app easier to read and tap: larger type and bigger touch targets throughout.`}]}];export{m as a,p as i,_ as n,g as r,h as t};